# Design context

Before introducing UI or changing shared components, tokens, responsive behavior, visual states, interface patterns, marketing copy, or brand usage:

1. Read `DESIGN.md` (orientation and source-of-truth table).
2. Read the relevant chapters of `docs/styles/design-system.md` (canonical intended design).

Runtime visual implementation is `src/app/globals.css` and the shared components. Current application code and tests govern product behavior. Do not treat inherited handbook paragraphs about the pre-adoption After Hours `DESIGN.md` or deleted `style-guide.md` pointer as current authority. Preserve supported light, dark, and system preferences.
